import PolicyLayout from '@/layouts/PolicyLayout.astro'
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Cookie policy"
  description="How seoskill.dev uses Clicky analytics, Cloudflare Turnstile, one first-visit cookie and one sign-in cookie on the account page."
  dateModified="2026-10-20"
>
  <h1>Cookie policy</h1>
  <p>Last updated: 20 October 2026</p>
  <p>
    The seoskill.dev website uses Clicky to count visits and see which pages
    people use. Clicky tracking cookies are disabled in the website code.
  </p>
  <p>
    Clicky receives normal browser and request information such as the page,
    referrer, device, and IP address under its{' '}
    <a href="https://clicky.com/terms/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">privacy policy</a>.
    It does not receive your local reports, tokens, connected account data, or
    provider responses.
  </p>
  <p>
    The site is served through Cloudflare. Cloudflare may also process normal
    web request data. Provider-backed forms use Cloudflare Turnstile as a
    strictly necessary security control against automated use. Turnstile
    processes challenge and browser information under Cloudflare's policies.
    It is not used for advertising or site analytics here.
  </p>
  <p>
    On your first visit, the site sets one first-party cookie, named <code>seo_first</code>,
    for 30 days. It holds the name of the site that
    sent you (such as a search engine, never the full address), the first
    page you opened and any campaign tags in that link. Later visits never
    change it, and it is not set when your browser sends Global Privacy
    Control. If you sign up for the hosted MCP server, it records this once,
    so we can see which paths bring people to SEO Skill. Nothing else reads
    it.
  </p>
  <p>
    The <a href="/account">account page</a> sets one strictly necessary
    cookie, named <code>seo_session</code>, when you sign in there with Google.
    It holds an encrypted reference to your account and is sent only to the
    account page. It lasts 30 days or until you sign out. The account page
    does not load Clicky.
  </p>
  <p>
    The <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> explains the short-lived daily
    quota counter and how the website and local SEO software handle data
    separately.
  </p>
  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Open an issue in the{' '}
    <a href="https://github.com/iannuttall/seo/issues">public GitHub repository</a>.
    Do not include tokens, private reports, personal data, or other secrets.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
